 \subsection{Multijet suppression and Preselection}
 \label{subsec:ch7_multijet}
 
-Multijet events can enter the SR and CR selections due to the mis-identified $\tau$ and $\met$ due to the poor jet resolution.
-Although a high $\met$ threshold rejects most of these events, the futher suppression is necessary due to their large cross section.
-As mentioned above, the high $\met$ is produced when an energetic jet is mismeasured. In this case, the direction of $\mpt$ is approximately towards that jet. Therefore a small $\Delta\phi$ between jet and $\mpt$ is expected.
-This contribution is referred to as fake $\met$. On the other hand, in signal events, the $\mpt$ from neutrinos have no such tendency.
+Multijet events can be selected in the SRs and CRs when a jet is misidentified as a $\tau$ and large $\met$ is produced by a jet-energy mismeasurement.
+Although most of these events are rejected by a high $\met$ threshold, further suppression is needed because of the large multijet cross section.
+When the $\pT$ of an energetic jet is underestimated, $\mpt$ points approximately towards that jet, so a small $\Delta\phi$ between the jet and $\mpt$ is expected.
+This contribution is referred to as fake $\met$.
+In signal events, no such tendency to align with a jet is expected for $\mpt$ from neutrinos.
 Figure~\ref{fig:ch7_fake_met} illustrates this difference.
 
